#### 1. Heuristic approach

This approach uses a set of heuristic values to determine the next best move. The board is represented as a 9-element vector in which each element is 2 (blank), 3 (X) or 5 (O). The program defines several functions to evaluate the board state and to make the next move based on heuristic values.

```text
function MAKE2():
    if central square is blank:
        return 5
    else:
        return any other square

function POSWIN(player):
    if player cannot win on the next move:
        return 0
    else:
        return square number of the winning move

function GO(square_number):
    make a move in the square specified by square_number

function PLAY():
    turn = 1
    while game is not over:
        if turn == 1:
            GO(1)
        else if turn == 2:
            if central square is blank: GO(5)
            else: GO(1)
        else if turn == 3:
            if top-right square is blank: GO(3)
            else: GO(3)
        else if turn >= 4:
            winning_move = POSWIN('X')
            if winning_move != 0:
                GO(winning_move)
            # more rules
        turn++
```

#### 2. Minimax algorithm

This approach recursively determines the optimal move by considering all possible future game states. It assigns a score to each game state based on the outcome and chooses the move that maximizes the player's score and minimizes the opponent's score.

The board is represented as a 9-element vector.

```text
function IS-TERMINAL(board):
    check if the game has ended (win, lose, draw)
    return true / false

function UTILITY(board):
    evaluate the utility (score) of the board
    return a score

function RESULT(board, move, player):
    return the new board state after making the move

function MINIMAX(board, player):
    if IS-TERMINAL(board):
        return UTILITY(board)
    if player == 'X':
        value = -infinity
        for each available move:
            new_board = RESULT(board, move, player)
            value = max(value, MINIMAX(new_board, 'O'))
        return value
    else:
        value = +infinity
        for each available move:
            new_board = RESULT(board, move, player)
            value = min(value, MINIMAX(new_board, 'X'))
        return value

function MAKE-MOVE(board, player):
    choose the available move with the best MINIMAX value
```
